diff --git a/docs/environment.md b/docs/environment.md
index 48966eb39..e7457de7e 100644
--- a/docs/environment.md
+++ b/docs/environment.md
@@ -181,6 +181,7 @@ stops the start with the variable, the supplied text and the accepted forms.
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_SLOTS` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. With `TF_FLASHNEXT_PEER_SLOTS=1` at `--tp 2`, a pass of up to 128 rows moves the out projection's two gathers (each rank's heads before it, each rank's output columns after it) by writing into the peer's mapped buffer and waiting on its flag instead of NCCL: the same bytes in the same places, so the same bits. Inert without `TF_FLASHNEXT_PEER_SLOTS` and outside `--tp 2`. Give every rank the same value. |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_EP_LOG` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1`: at `--tp 2` each eager decode or verify window of up to 64 rows copies its layers' expert picks aside and reads them back once at its end (a sync a window); every 64 windows each rank logs the mean and p90 of the distinct routed experts it computed a layer, its pairs a layer, and the mean gap between the ranks in distinct experts and in pairs. Captured windows and prompt fills are not counted. Replies are unchanged. |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_OVERLAP` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. `1` at `--tp 2` on one host with `TF_FLASHNEXT_OWNER_SLOTS=1`: a prompt chunk of at least 2,048 rows runs as two halves, layer by layer, the first half's layer before the second's. Each half's owner-slot exchange and sums gather run on a second stream and a second NCCL communicator (its own connections) after its experts, while the pass's stream computes the other half; a half waits for its exchange before its next layer. The kernels and bytes are those of two chunks of those rows, so the bits are the same. Half B's scratch (half a chunk) is held from load. Inert without the owner-slot exchange, with `TF_FLASHNEXT_HIDDEN_SUM`, across hosts, at `--pp 2` and one rank. Give every rank the same value. |
+| `TF_FLASHNEXT_OVERLAP_OUTPROJ` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. With `TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_OVERLAP=1`, each half's DeltaNet and attention out projection (its input gather, column copies, matmul and output gather) also runs on the side stream and communicator, and the halves interleave by half layers: A's mixer, B's mixer, A's experts, B's experts. A half's expert read-out waits for its out projection. The same launches and bytes, so the same bits. Inert without the overlap. Give every rank the same value. |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_OUTPROJ_KSPLIT` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off. **Not bit-exact.** `1` at `--tp 2` under the dense split: each rank loads the input columns of every DeltaNet `out_proj` and attention `o_proj` that its own heads feed, runs the projection over its heads alone into a full-width FP32 partial, and one exchange adds the two partials (the peer's mapped buffer with `TF_FLASHNEXT_PEER_SLOTS` for a pass of up to 128 rows, else an NCCL sum). That replaces the two gathers around the projection with one sync a layer. The slice sums meet as (slices 0-3) + (slices 4-7) instead of in one chain, so outputs differ slightly from off; both ranks still hold identical bits, since `a + b` equals `b + a`. Gate it on token match against the reference and a quality check. Inert at `--pp 2` and one rank. Give every rank the same value. |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_READOUT_ROWS` | Whole row count; default 64; `0` never takes the tiles |
 | `TF_FLASHNEXT_CHUNK` | Whole prompt rows a pass, 1 through 16384; default 3072 |
